.TH SOVRD "1" "August 2026" "Soveroot experimental node" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sovrd \- run the experimental Soveroot node daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sovrd
.B \-chain=labnet
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sovrd
is the headless daemon for the experimental Soveroot reference implementation.
It validates and relays blocks and transactions and exposes RPC, REST, and
optional ZMQ services.
.PP
This build can start only the isolated, non-production
.BR labnet .
The chain must be selected explicitly with
.BR \-chain=labnet .
Inherited Bitcoin mainnet, testnet, signet, and regtest parameters are retained
only as non-startable compatibility fixtures and are rejected by the application
isolation interlock. Labnet coins have no monetary value.
.PP
The proposed Soveroot proof-of-work candidate is isolated research code and is
not part of labnet consensus. Run
.B sovrd \-help
for the complete option list emitted by this build.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-chain=labnet
Select the only startable network in this experimental fork.
.TP
.B \-conf=FILE
Read configuration from FILE. The inherited default filename remains
.I bitcoin.conf
until a separately reviewed data-path migration is adopted.
.TP
.B \-datadir=DIR
Store node data beneath DIR. Labnet data uses the
.I dcp-labnet
network subdirectory.
.TP
.B \-daemon
Run in the background where supported.
.TP
.B \-help
Print the complete, build-specific help text and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version and licensing information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start an isolated labnet daemon:
.PP
.EX
sovrd -chain=labnet -daemon
.EE
.PP
Query it with the RPC client:
.PP
.EX
sovr-cli -chain=labnet getblockchaininfo
.EE
.SH SAFETY
Soveroot is experimental software. This repository does not provide a live
monetary network, production release, token sale, or security guarantee. Do not
use labnet wallets or keys to protect assets of value.
